  "description": "MEJVEE crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C196 H137 Gd14 N54 O67 5+,2.5(C1 O3 2-),0.5(C12 H8 N2),26(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd4 (Gd) has 9 O neighbors; Gd5 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd6 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd7 (Gd) has 6 O neighbors; Gd8 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd9 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd10 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd11 (Gd) has 4 O neighbors; Gd12 (Gd) has 5 O neighbors; Gd13 (Gd) has 5 O neighbors; Gd14 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 20 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.747-4.776 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 91.40-155.70°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Gd14(CO3)13(ccnm)9(OH)(H2O)6(phen)13(NO3)](CO3)2.5·(phen)0.5·26H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 6 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
